&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;India is home to a large and rapidly evolving base of digital businesses. SaaS companies, e-commerce businesses, platforms, marketplaces, and AI-first companies are scaling quickly, serving increasingly sophisticated customers, and expanding beyond India.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Commercial &amp;amp; SMB team partners with high-potential businesses at an important stage of their growth. Some are already using Stripe and can benefit from a deeper partnership. Others are evaluating how to modernize their payments and financial infrastructure. Our role is to understand their ambitions, help them make well-informed decisions, and bring together the right capabilities across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-cycle sales role with meaningful ownership. You will create pipeline, win new users, expand existing relationships, and help shape Stripe’s commercial strategy in India. You will join a focused, entrepreneurial team in Bengaluru while working closely with colleagues across Stripe’s global Product, Solutions Architecture, Customer Success, Risk, Legal, Finance, and Operations organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a portfolio of high-potential commercial and small-to-medium businesses across India. You will operate with a dual mandate: acquire new users and grow existing relationships through greater adoption, new use cases, and long-term strategic value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute a territory plan focused on high-potential Indian SaaS companies, digital-native businesses, e-commerce companies, platforms, marketplaces, and global-first businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate your own pipeline through thoughtful outbound engagement, referrals, ecosystem relationships, events, partnerships, and rigorous account research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the complete sales cycle, from prospecting and discovery through solution design, commercial negotiation, contracting, and launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop trusted relationships with founders and senior stakeholders across finance, product, engineering, operations, and procurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand each user’s business model, growth priorities, technical architecture, and current financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex customer needs into clear solutions and business cases, connecting Stripe’s capabilities to measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for new product adoption, deeper integrations, improved payment performance, new business models, and international expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead compelling product and solution conversations in partnership with Solutions Architecture and other specialists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate multi-stakeholder decisions involving commercial, technical, operational, risk, and regulatory considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate pricing and commercial terms with sound judgment, balancing user value, competitive context, and Stripe’s long-term objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage pipeline and forecasting with rigor, using data to prioritize accounts and maintain a clear view of risks, dependencies, and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Customer Success and cross-functional teams to ensure a strong transition from sale to implementation and long-term adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring structured market and user feedback to Stripe’s Product, Marketing, and leadership teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe in India’s technology and business ecosystem, building relationships with founders, investors, accelerators, partners, and industry communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, success means:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating a healthy, self-generated pipeline in priority segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Winning high-quality new users and expanding existing relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increasing adoption of relevant Stripe products and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building senior relationships that position Stripe as a long-term strategic partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running disciplined sales cycles with clear qualification, strong business cases, accurate forecasting, and effective close plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping Stripe develop a sharper understanding of India’s commercial and SMB opportunity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in full-cycle, consultative B2B technology sales, including meaningful experience in the Indian market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated track record of generating pipeline and closing new-business or expansion opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to founders or senior stakeholders across finance, product, technology, or operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong discovery, qualification, and solution-selling skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical products and translate complex requirements into clear customer and business value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgment, including experience building business cases and leading pricing and contract negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical discipline and comfort using data to prioritize a territory, assess opportunities, and forecast accurately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple sales cycles at different stages without compromising quality or customer trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating complex work across multiple internal teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate with ownership, resilience, and sound judgment in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, SaaS, cloud, developer tools, e-commerce, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to digital-native businesses, SaaS companies, platforms, marketplaces, or companies expanding internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships within India’s founder, technology, venture capital, or business ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with APIs, online payments, subscription business models, fraud prevention, platforms, or cross-border commerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling multiple products or solutions into the same customer relationship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a global organization with geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with spreadsheets, CRM analytics, SQL, or a demonstrated willingness to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commercial and SMB businesses represent an important part of India’s digital economy and Stripe’s long-term opportunity in the market. In this role, you will help ambitious businesses strengthen their financial infrastructure, launch new products, and expand internationally. You will also help build the sales motion, relationships, and market understanding that will shape Stripe’s growth in India for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Platform Sales team works with B2B Software Platforms to help them facilitate payments for their customers using our Stripe Connect product. Software Platforms, also known as B2B Indirect, are software platform businesses who serve other businesses. Platforms already using Stripe include Shopify, Lightspeed and Mindbody. The team’s mission is to help SaaS Platforms use financial services to enhance their mission.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key member to the Stripe Platforms team, you will navigate complex organizations and identify ways Stripe can exceed expectations. We’re building something new, developing our sales process, our value proposition and assisting in the creation of key tools and assets, we’re looking for pioneers to join us on this adventure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Platform Account Executive for India, you will create partnerships between Stripe and the most innovative and fastest-growing software platforms in the world by helping them to understand how Stripe’s online commerce infrastructure can make payments a competitive advantage for their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will navigate complex organisations and identify ways Stripe can help them monetise financial services across their business. We’re building this specialisation with the need to develop our sales process, refine the value proposition and create a localised set of key tools and assets. We’re looking for experienced sales executives to join us on this adventure!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a named account list and develop account plans for winning and expanding business with mid-market and enterprise SaaS and Fintech companies in the India region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle from lead to close for upper middle market and enterprise companies to showcase Stripe value in competitive processes, and consultatively apply highly-technical product knowledge from Stripe solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and engage with high-potential prospective SaaS Platforms, building long term, strategic relationships with them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leaders from multiple functions (e.g., Engineering, Product, and Finance) at existing and prospective users to lead complex product workshops and financial analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop outbound strategies to create and nurture opportunities within India&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain key relationships with C-level executives, while orchestrating the right executive touch points as well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop relationships with executive stakeholders at new and existing clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an adept Enterprise salesperson, capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization, including the CTO, COO, and CFO. You have experience working with upper middle market and enterprise companies. You get excited about prospecting, and are capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish. You have an in-depth understanding of the buyer journey and can lead a complex, multi-party sale in a highly consultative manner. You are used to building value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require deep product understanding, combined with technical knowledge. You are naturally analytical and enjoy digging into business models and helping customers quantify their investment decisions. Finally, you enjoy building – you like to actively participate in the development of our sales process, the articulation of our value proposition, and the creation of key tools and assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of software sales experience selling to large users in the India market, preferably at a technology company, with a track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the India domestic and cross-border business landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of moving sales processes forward from inception to close by leading complex, multi-party sales. SaaS Platforms are trusting Stripe to help them monetise financial services, and you have demonstrated a consultative approach to sales, are quick to understand their potential monetisation strategy, and are able to help your prospects articulate the value proposition of embedding financial services to create a SaaS Platform business unit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great listening skills and ability to quickly become a trusted resource for decision-makers across technology and finance orgs within software companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to understand complex technical problems and understand how Stripe’s solutions can address them. You are confident in understanding Stripe’s API and having technical discussion with support from Stripe engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and understanding of existing and developing payments technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the India Startups team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;India is producing a new generation of SaaS companies, digital-native businesses, platforms, marketplaces, and AI-first startups with global ambitions. These businesses need more than a payments provider. They need financial infrastructure that can support rapid growth, international expansion, new products, and increasingly complex business models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Startups Grower team helps Stripe’s largest and fastest-growing startup users realize more value from Stripe. We combine commercial ownership with deep curiosity about our users’ businesses. We work with founders, CFOs, product leaders, and engineering teams to understand where they are going next, then bring together the right people and products across Stripe to help them get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to shape how Stripe serves India’s most ambitious technology companies. You will join a focused, entrepreneurial team in Bengaluru while working closely with colleagues across Stripe’s global Product, Solutions Architecture, Customer Success, Risk, Legal, Finance, and Operations organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own and grow a portfolio of high-potential startup customers. Your goal will be to build trusted, long-term relationships, retain and expand existing revenue, and help users adopt the Stripe products that best support their next phase of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of each user’s business model, growth plans, technical architecture, and financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with founders and senior stakeholders across finance, product, engineering, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create account plans that identify retention risks, expansion opportunities, decision-makers, and clear paths to measurable user value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead renewals and commercial negotiations with a focus on durable partnerships, strong outcomes for users, and responsible revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and close opportunities for additional product adoption, new use cases, deeper integrations, and international expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run thoughtful discovery and product conversations that connect Stripe’s capabilities to outcomes such as revenue growth, improved conversion, fraud reduction, faster launches, and greater operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a portfolio with rigor, using data to prioritize accounts, forecast accurately, and focus time on the opportunities with the greatest potential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute scaled campaigns for groups of users with similar needs while maintaining a high-quality, consultative experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate across Solutions Architecture, Customer Success, Product, Risk, Legal, Finance, and Operations to resolve complex issues and set users up for long-term success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring structured feedback from Indian startups to Stripe’s Product and leadership teams, helping improve our products, positioning, and market strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships across India’s startup ecosystem, including founders, investors, accelerators, and technology communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, success means:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retaining and growing a portfolio of strategic startup users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increasing adoption of relevant Stripe products and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building senior, trusted relationships that extend beyond a single transaction or renewal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying opportunities early and leading them to a clear commercial outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating a predictable, high-quality operating rhythm across account planning, pipeline management, forecasting, and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping Stripe better understand and serve high-growth companies building from India for the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a commercially strong, intellectually curious account executive who enjoys helping high-growth companies solve important problems. You can move comfortably between a founder conversation, a technical discovery session, a pricing discussion, and an internal strategy review. You are equally comfortable going deep on a small number of strategic opportunities and executing at pace across a broader portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the minimum requirements, we encourage you to apply. Preferred qualifications are helpful, but they are not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in account management, consultative sales, customer growth, or another client-facing commercial role, including meaningful experience in the Indian market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated track record of retaining and expanding relationships with technology companies or other complex B2B customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading renewals, upsells, cross-sells, or multi-product commercial negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong discovery skills and the ability to translate business and technical priorities into relevant solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build credibility with founders and senior stakeholders across finance, product, and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgment, including comfort with pricing, business cases, contracts, and competing customer priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical discipline and the ability to use data to prioritize a portfolio, build account strategies, and forecast accurately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating complex work across multiple internal teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate with ownership and sound judgment in an ambiguous, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, SaaS, cloud, developer tools, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with venture-backed startups, digital-native companies, SaaS businesses, platforms, marketplaces, or businesses expanding internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships within India’s founder, venture capital, accelerator, or technology ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with APIs, online payments, subscription business models, fraud prevention, platforms, or cross-border commerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a global organization with geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with spreadsheets, CRM analytics, SQL, or a demonstrated willingness to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;India’s most ambitious startups are building products for customers across the world. In this role, you will help those companies develop the financial infrastructure they need to scale, while shaping Stripe’s relationships and long-term growth in India. The work combines commercial impact, technical problem-solving, ecosystem building, and the opportunity to partner with some of India’s most exciting founders and technology teams.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance Operations (FinOps) team provides and enhances core business services that are the backbone for Stripe. FinOps uses data and operational excellence to deliver technology solutions, procurement, billing and payroll services, strategic sourcing, and supplier relationship management to Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Monetization Operations Analyst to join our growing team. This individual will help us improve user experience through accurate and timely onboarding of contracts, workflows and deliver improvements in our integrated financial systems with business partners, financial colleagues, and engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for onboarding sold custom contracts into our billing systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand the legal languages of the contract and comfortable working on it and have strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable and auditable onboarding processes for new and existing users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal systems, deal desk, legal, sales ops, internal audit, go-to-market, engineer and account managers to develop and improve the process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with account managers to solve user inquiries related to onboarding implementation, billing, and collections and if needed troubleshoot as well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze our processes and instigate changes to help scale our operations and improve user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with other Stripe teams to assist with system implementations for billings, collections, and assist with internal and external ad-hoc audit support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help scale and optimize our processes by assisting with the execution of key projects and programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain unique insights into various businesses on Stripe scale and operate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can quickly learn the Stripe ways of working and make a real impact through process enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a part of building a brand-new team and operational culture for Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with monthly and quarterly flux analysis of key metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with ad hoc projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-5&amp;nbsp; years of relevant financial operations/billing experience or 3+ years of customer service experience with a degree in Business Administration, Finance, or relevant field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and organizational skills, both written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills and demonstrated ability to work independently, analyze problems and data sets to make complex investigation decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of gSuite tools, Salesforce and MS-Office products and experience working with/analyzing contracts and large data sets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently analyze and evaluate information from various data sources to determine a course of action for a matched case&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history of taking on various types of challenging projects and producing results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution-oriented mindset with enthusiasm for establishing best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-disciplined, diligent, proactive and detail oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will also likely have (not required):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge in payments and the fintech industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to be flexible and comfortable with changing requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder&#39;s mindset and a willingness to question assumptions and conventional wisdom&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for creating new systems and solving problems via infrastructure and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Accounting team at Stripe supports products across Stripe by providing guidance on accounting implications and enabling teams to make informed strategic decisions. The team records business transactions accurately and on time in the balance sheet and income statement, and partners with cross-functional and international teams in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is seeking an experienced accountant to join our world-class accounting team, focusing on products developed by our Bridge subsidiary. You’ll leverage your technical expertise with U.S. GAAP to identify accounting implications and customer impacts and advise cross-functional partners. You will be responsible for ensuring timely and accurate month-end close results for Bridge products, while also working on initiatives to create scalable accounting solutions..&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and perform monthly close activities, including journal entries, reconciliations, analytic reviews, and financial reporting deliverables for Bridge products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, recommend and implement scalable accounting processes to support global growth at Bridge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our business and finance teams to understand new products, features, and contracts, and advise on accounting implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Internal Systems and Engineering teams to improve financial systems and automate accounting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the effectiveness of internal controls and design processes and controls for emerging business activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand data and system flows, analyzing financial results to identify and address anomalies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support external audit processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant public accounting and/or industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional accountancy qualification, such as CA, CPA, ACA, ACCA, or CIMA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of US GAAP and experience with internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with monthly or quarterly close processes, journal-entry preparation and posting, audits, regulatory reporting, financial-statement preparation, and accounting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills, with the ability to convey financial concepts to both financial and non-financial audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to structure ambiguous work and build systems and automation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the technology or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience accounting for cryptocurrencies, including stablecoins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Oracle Suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data-querying and analysis tools, including SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to relevant US GAAP standards, e.g. ASC 860, ASC 606, or ASC 326, is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To further this important mission, we&#39;re building our Accounting team in Bangalore Finance and are looking for someone to help us scale for the future in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly detail-oriented and tech-forward Corporate Accounting Analyst to join our fast-paced corporate accounting team. In this role, you will play a critical part in managing General Ledger (GL) activities, ensuring accurate close processes, and driving accounting precision across specialized technical areas, including debt, prepaids, intercompany transactions, and lease accounting .&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate holds a &lt;strong&gt;Chartered Accountant (CA)&lt;/strong&gt; qualification, possesses &lt;strong&gt;4–6 years of progressive accounting experience&lt;/strong&gt;, and brings a modern, tech-enabled mindset—specifically the ability to leverage AI tools, automation, and advanced analytics to streamline workflows and solve complex accounting problems in a rapidly evolving environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end accounting schedules, journal entries, and balance sheet reconciliations for corporate accounting areas .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage month-end, quarter-end, and year-end closing activities within prescribed timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct variance analyses on P&amp;amp;L and Balance Sheet line items, investigating unexpected fluctuations and providing actionable commentary to management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audit requests by preparing audit schedules, supporting documentation, and clear accounting workpapers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams (F&amp;amp;S, FinOps, Tax, Operations) to ensure accurate accounting treatment for complex transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage&lt;strong&gt; ERP automation, analytical capabilities&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;AI-driven tools &lt;/strong&gt;(e.g., prompt engineering, automated reconciliation workflows, intelligent data extraction) to enhance accuracy and timeliness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify bottlenecks in the financial close cycle and implement automated solutions or streamlined workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize advanced data tools to process large volumes of financial data accurately under tight deadliness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Certification:&lt;/strong&gt; Chartered Accountant (CA) or equivalent professional accounting designation is &lt;strong&gt;mandatory&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;4 to 6 years&lt;/strong&gt; of post-qualification core corporate accounting experience, with strong hands-on expertise in General Ledger operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; Tech Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to adopt and operate AI tools (e.g., generative AI for documentation/analysis, workflow automation software, advanced ERP modules) to optimize accounting tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Competencies &amp;amp; Soft Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast-Paced Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to prioritize effectively, meet tight monthly/quarterly closing deadlines, and thrive in an agile, dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Detail-Oriented:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional problem-solving skills with a high degree of precision in numerical and technical accounting work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Clear verbal and written communication skills to effectively collaborate with remote teams, management, and external auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-Starter:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong ownership mindset, able to work independently as a contractor with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of (or experience in) the technology or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Big4 working experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oracle suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hubble and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe was built with simplicity in mind. We strive to deliver frictionless experiences for all of our users, whether they are an Independent Business, Startup, SMB, or Enterprise and our mission is to provide all Stripe Users with the best support experience possible. Today, Stripe handles over a million support cases per year and processes millions of internal transactions.&amp;nbsp; We’re going to achieve excellence by thinking of support in a novel, solution-oriented way, and viewing operations as an integral enabler of all of Stripe’s growth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is launching Stripe Delivery Centers - a brand new global team to design, implement and grow Stripe’s operations for the next decade. We are looking for dynamic and curious people that have a passion for solving global user issues, building operations, drive process improvement and want to play a front-line role in building this new operational capability for Stripe and accelerating Stripe’s growth. If you like challenging, scaled problems and are an amazing teammate, we want to hear from you!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The credit risk operations team plays a critical role in ensuring a healthy financial ecosystem for businesses around the world. This team will directly impact the company’s bottom line and growth capabilities by supporting new and emerging businesses. The Credit Operations team is responsible for conducting credit risk assessments, underwriting small and mid-size users, and proposing mitigation strategies that enable Stripe to take smart risks for our users.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work with merchants, from successful venture-backed startups to well established institutions; evaluating their business models and financial statements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Help manage Stripe’s portfolio by developing a deep understanding of risk across industries, geographies, and operating models&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Identify differing risks of complex business models and enforce appropriate loss mitigation actions based on your assessment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Utilize analytics to optimize strategies which can be enforced across Stripe’s portfolio&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Identify risk factors and trends and further report these identifiers to the wider risk team to ensure consistency in partnership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Identify gaps in current systems, policies and strategies, and recommend enhancements and process improvements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Have an opportunity to learn how Stripe operates from ground up and make a real impact on the future on organization&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Be a part of building a brand new team and operational culture for Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Partner with global operations specialists or business process owners to run a critical workflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A minimum of 2+ years of experience with knowledge of commercial credit underwriting, financial risk modeling and cash flow forecasting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability to transform business and financial data into a cohesive narrative that outlines potential credit risks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Strong knowledge of accounting principles and comfort with evaluating financial statements and business models across a range of industries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You excel in analytical thinking and problem solving&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You have a process-oriented mindset and ability to get things done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You enjoy working in an in-office environment with strong cross team collaboration and support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You are able to prioritize and enjoy working in a quick-moving environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You are humble and have a proven track record for working well across teams and with external partners&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You’re willing to work (no more than) one weekend day each month - you’ll receive a weekday off the following week; the SDC operates during daytime hours with shifts from the morning through early evening&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree/diploma in Finance or Accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, e-commerce, or fintech mitigating credit risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Data Science and Analytics organization at Stripe partners with teams across the company to drive rigorous, data-informed decision-making at scale. Within this org, the Verifications and Greater China data teams deliver critical analytical and data science work—from identity verification and risk modeling to market-specific growth insights—that directly shapes Stripe&#39;s ability to serve users safely and expand into new markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, the team comprises individual contributors distributed across Singapore and India, supporting two high-impact pillars. We&#39;re looking for a founding Data Science Manager based in Bengaluru to build and lead this growing regional footprint from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare 0 → 1 leadership role with a dual mandate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pillar 1—Direct Team Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Manage a team of Data Scientists and Data Analysts (currently 4 individual contributors across India and Singapore) spanning the Verifications and Greater China workstreams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Own roadmap prioritization, execution quality, and stakeholder alignment for both workstreams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Drive hiring for open and future roles in India, building a high-caliber data team in a competitive talent market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Foster individual contributor growth through real-time coaching, mentorship, career development, and performance management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pillar 2—Regional Data Craft Lead (India Office)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Serve as the founding data craft leader for Stripe&#39;s India office. Set quality standards, establish community rituals (knowledge sharing, peer reviews, office hours), and cultivate a strong local data culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Act as the go-to point of contact for data craft standards, tooling, and best practices for co-located analysts, even those outside your direct reporting line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Partner with managers and leads across the broader Data org to ensure consistency in methodology, tooling, and quality bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Support onboarding and integration of new data hires in the Bengaluru office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Over time, this role has the potential to evolve into a Center of Excellence (COE) model—becoming the single point of data leadership in India across multiple product pillars (e.g., Payments, Growth, Marketing), not just Risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Build, manage, and develop a high-performing, geographically distributed data team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Define and drive the data roadmap in close partnership with product, engineering, and business stakeholders—ensuring analytical work is tightly coupled to business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Establish and raise the bar on analytical rigor, experimentation frameworks, and data science best practices across the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Recruit and retain skilled data talent, crafting a compelling hiring narrative anchored in local leadership and craft excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Champion a culture of technical excellence, intellectual curiosity, and operational discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Collaborate with cross-functional partners and other data leaders globally to align priorities, share learnings, and maintain org-wide consistency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Communicate insights, recommendations, and team progress clearly to senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• 10+ years of experience in data science, analytics, or a related quantitative field, with 3+ years in a people management role leading data scientists or analysts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Strong technical foundation in SQL, Python or R, statistical modeling, and experimentation design&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Demonstrated ability to translate ambiguous business problems into structured analytical frameworks and actionable insights&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience managing and developing individual contributor talent across multiple levels, including coaching, career pathing, and performance management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills—able to influence without authority across functions and time zones along with proven ability to drive alignment and execution across distributed, cross-functional teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Advanced degree (M.S. or Ph.D.) in a quantitative discipline such as Statistics, Economics, Computer Science, Mathematics, or a related field&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience working in the payments, fintech, or financial services industry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Prior experience building and scaling data teams in a high-growth environment—particularly standing up 0 → 1 functions or teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Track record of being a builder who has personally architected the rituals, standards, hiring bar, and craft culture for a data team from the ground up&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Familiarity with risk, verifications, or compliance-related data domains&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Experience operating across Asia-Pacific markets and navigating the nuances of multi-region team management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Passion for developing others and creating environments where individual contributors do the best work of their careers&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Revenue &amp;amp; Financial Management group is building new products that expand the scope of problems we tackle beyond payments into Revenue Management, Financial Operations and analytics. Right now this includes products like Billing, Invoicing, Revenue Recognition, Reconciliation and the underlying platform for batch and real time processing of large scale financial data to power these solutions. These solutions are going to be key pillars for Stripe’s growing SaaS business and a major revenue stream.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced engineering manager to lead the team building the foundation for accounting system and user-facing product features that will streamline and automate accrual accounting for Stripe customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead your team of talented engineers to solve data engineering challenges at scale and deliver a high level of technical and operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers and talk to directly to customers to drive a high-impact, prioritized roadmap for your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, coach, mentor, develop, and grow engineers on your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be deeply involved in launching new product features and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineers and product managers across Stripe to ensure your features are integrated into the Stripe suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to engineering initiatives across the Revenue and Finance Automation (RFA) organization and across Stripe as a member of Stripe’s engineering management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience and 10+ years of overall experience in the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully led high-complexity teams, working in parallel on multiple high-impact areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works very well cross-functionally, and is able to think rigorously and make hard decisions and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourages a healthy work environment that’s both supportive and challenging and enables engineers to do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background and hands-on experience in solving large scale and difficult technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Values and enjoys working with a diverse group of people with different expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with large scale distributed systems or big data processing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in high-growth teams similar to Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building financial systems or tools for financial experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with accounting procedures or systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Infrastructure is responsible for the reliability, scale, performance, and cost of Stripe’s systems and the productivity and sentiment of Stripe’s people. You may work on a wide variety of critical business areas within Core Infrastructure. We’re the home for Stripe&#39;s critical tier0 infrastructure systems (Compute, Networking, DocumentDB, Distributed Caching and High assurance engineering). We build the foundational platform for Stripe products and services to allow them to operate at scale. We drive reliability, availability, efficiency and scalability of these systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager in Core Infrastructure at Stripe, you will lead a team solving challenging distributed systems problems and drive critical improvements in our foundational platform.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with senior leadership to define and execute strategic initiatives for Stripe&#39;s core infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading and mentoring a team of experienced engineers, fostering their growth and career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving technical decisions and architectural improvements for large-scale, distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with product and engineering teams across Stripe to identify and implement infrastructure solutions that enhance scalability, reliability, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivating a culture of engineering excellence, innovation, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the engineering team in achieving a high level of technical quality, reliability, and ease-of-use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruiting great engineers, in collaboration with Stripe&#39;s recruiting team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of industry experience in software engineering, with at least 3-4 years in engineering management roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in designing, building, and operating large-scale distributed systems and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with cloud technologies, preferably AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in multiple areas of infrastructure, such as compute, networking, databases, caching systems, or storage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of leading and growing high-performing engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in managing geographically distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to influence and collaborate across all levels of the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a data-driven approach to decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive technical strategy and roadmap planning for complex infrastructure systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with globally distributed systems and multi-region architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with containerization and orchestration technologies (e.g., Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of performance optimization and capacity planning for large-scale systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in scaling infrastructure platforms to handle millions of requests per second (RPS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of successful cross-functional project leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with programming languages commonly used in infrastructure, such as Go, Ruby, or Java.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Internal Systems Automations Platform team’s mission is to unlock productivity across all of Stripe’s internal systems. We build solutions to transform core processes for Finance, Accounting, People, Legal, Sales, Marketing, and more. We orchestrate the full automation lifecycle, using artificial intelligence (AI) for planning, analysis, and reasoning, and deterministic scripts, code, and pipelines for reliable and trustworthy execution. We enable technical and nontechnical users to build hybrid code and no-code automations while working with central Operations, Developer Productivity, Infrastructure, and machine learning (ML) teams on behalf of all Internal Systems customers to build powerful platforms together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced engineering manager with a passion for simplifying complex systems and driving operational efficiency. In this role, you’ll analyze existing processes across Stripe’s internal systems, use automation platforms where possible, and design new solutions when needed. You will implement cutting-edge automation solutions, including AI agents, robotic process automation (RPA), and data pipelines, and build best-in-class platforms. You’ll be responsible for continuously improving workflows to maximize efficiency and deliver meaningful business impact across a broad set of internal stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead your team of talented engineers to design and deploy data pipelines and intelligent workflows that simplify operations for internal customers, including Finance, Accounting, Legal, People, Sales, Marketing, and Operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers and talk directly with users to drive a high-impact, prioritized roadmap for your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, coach, mentor, develop, and grow engineers on your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be deeply involved in launching new product features and capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineers and product managers across Stripe to ensure your features are integrated into the Stripe suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience and 10+ years of overall experience in the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience working on high-scale systems with a strong technical foundation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works very well cross-functionally and is able to think rigorously and make hard decisions and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourages a healthy work environment that’s both supportive and challenging and enables engineers to do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background and hands-on experience in solving large-scale and difficult technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with diverse internal teams and stakeholders across Finance, Legal, Operations, and other business functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI, large language model (LLM), or ML technologies is highly valuable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of context-driven AI agents that can autonomously figure out solutions when given business problems and context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

