&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;At Okta, Demo Engineering bridges the gap between product innovation and go-to-market execution—acting as a global force multiplier for our technical sales organization. We equip internal and partner Solution Engineers worldwide with the tools and environments needed to effortlessly demonstrate how Okta secures identities across workforces, customers, and AI agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, your code directly powers Okta’s global sales engine. The demo architectures and interactive experiences you create will be leveraged by hundreds of field engineers across dozens of countries, influencing thousands of enterprise customer conversations. Operating within an engineering-first, collaborative culture focused on automation, modularity, and self-service, you will build the core platform that makes Okta’s field teams faster, sharper, and more scalable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect Reusable Assets:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and develop modular demo components and pre-configured product environments tailored to high-impact, solution-driven customer scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capture Field Insights:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with global field teams to gather &quot;Voice of the Customer&quot; feedback—translating prospect expectations, preferences, and friction points into platform improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Platform Adoption:&lt;/strong&gt; Team up with Field Readiness to champion the Demo Platform and accelerate usage across the broader go-to-market organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure &amp;amp; Optimize:&lt;/strong&gt; Build telemetry, analytics, and reporting dashboards to monitor demo engagement and quantify field impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launch New Capabilities:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate cross-functionally with Product Management and Core Engineering to build demo-ready experiences ahead of new product releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence Product Roadmap:&lt;/strong&gt; Represent field and customer insights during release planning to help shape future product direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable the Field:&lt;/strong&gt; Author clear technical walkthroughs, demonstration guides, and video tutorials to empower self-service adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring to the Table&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science/Engineering or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years of hands-on software development experience building Enterprise SaaS solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-Stack &amp;amp; Cloud Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;React.js&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Node.js&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;AWS Serverless&lt;/strong&gt; architectures (Lambda, DynamoDB, SQS, SNS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-Tenant Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven background designing and implementing multi-tenant systems with strict tenant isolation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DevOps &amp;amp; Automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience with Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) or automated configuration management tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity &amp;amp; API Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid experience integrating REST/GraphQL APIs with identity providers, backed by strong working knowledge of modern authentication and authorization standards (&lt;strong&gt;OAuth 2.0, OIDC, SAML&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Globally Minded:&lt;/strong&gt; Experienced in collaborating across time zones and supporting a distributed, international field organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proactive Builder:&lt;/strong&gt; Self-driven and resourceful—you spot gaps, propose solutions, and execute without needing micromanagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Connector:&lt;/strong&gt; Energized by working at the intersection of Sales, Product, and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Thinker:&lt;/strong&gt; Capable of balancing fast-turnaround field requests with long-term architectural scalability and code reuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer-Obsessed:&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled at distilling qualitative customer and field feedback into concrete technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience on a Demo Engineering, Technical Marketing, or Developer Relations team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in Presales, Solutions Engineering, or Customer-Facing Technical Consulting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on familiarity with &lt;strong&gt;Okta&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;Auth0&lt;/strong&gt; platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
