&lt;p&gt;The MongoDB Documentation team is a group of writers and engineers who develop and maintain the documentation for the MongoDB product family. Our goal is to help our readers, both humans and AI, successfully use MongoDB products by providing outstanding documentation. The MongoDB Documentation team is a part of the MongoDB Core Product organization and is tightly integrated with the engineering teams responsible for each product.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Docs team is responsible for documenting all aspects of the MongoDB data platform including the database, query language, Atlas, Vector Search, VoyageAI models, Full-Text Search, Stream Processing, client libraries, administrative tools, connectors, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your AI-forward mindset coupled with strong writing and technical skills will create clear reference docs and tutorials on high-complexity features. Your work, along with the other two MongoDB Docs teams, support AI agents, answer engines, and a large global community of new and experienced MongoDB users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to speak to candidates who are based in Gurgaon, Bengaluru or Mumbai for our hybrid working model.&lt;/p&gt;
