&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;br&gt;Visit druva.com and follow us on LinkedIn, X and Facebook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Druva is seeking to hire a Sales Engineer with a focus on Data Protection with AI &amp;amp;amp;Data Security. As a Sales Engineer, you will provide technical direction and business guidance to the regional sales teams. We are looking for a motivated and proactive&lt;br&gt;individual to help exceed sales targets by driving innovative technical programs, conducting customer demonstrations, POCs, and overseeing daily technical solutioning activities. You will be responsible for evangelizing, positioning, and&lt;br&gt;architecting Druva’s Data Protection, AI &amp;amp;amp; Data Security Solutions to a mix of new &amp;amp;amp; existing customer accounts in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrates technical leadership and subject matter expertise on fully managed cloud-native SaaS, Endpoint &amp;amp;amp; Server Data Protection, AI &amp;amp;amp; Data Security, and Cyber Resiliency&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Provides technical leadership and direction to customers and internal staff in the development of Druva solutions, supporting pre-sales activities within the assigned region&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Leverage technical discovery and qualification fundamentals to establish rapport as a trusted advisor to develop and propose solutions that meet the technology and business requirements of prospective &amp;amp;amp; existing customer accounts in the region&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Meet business objectives by collaborating with Sales Executives in the region&lt;br&gt;• Assist in delivering technical enablement to the Druva Channel Partner ecosystem&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp;5 &amp;nbsp;to 8 years in technical customer-facing roles with at least 2+ years as a sales engineer working with enterprise software solutions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of enterprise server backup technologies&lt;br&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of Virtualization Platforms VMWare, HyperV, Nutanix &amp;amp;amp; ProxMox.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of Databases such as MS-SQL, Oracle, Azure SQL.&lt;br&gt;• Working knowledge &amp;amp;amp; understanding of AI concepts and tools. Hands on knowledge of Claude, Copilot would be added advantage.&lt;br&gt;• Intermediate level knowledge of operating systems, including MS Windows, Linux,&amp;amp; amp; macOS.&lt;br&gt;• Experience with Active Directory, Entra ID, SSO, MFA, SCCM, and automated deployment tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate level of knowledge of industry AI.&lt;br&gt;• Basic understanding of network technologies and protocols – TCP/IP, VLAN, DNS, switches, firewalls, routers, and proxies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Entrepreneurial - willing to go the extra mile, strong work ethic, resourceful, “get it&lt;br&gt;done” attitude&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• A highly energetic drive to meet goals with a strong hands-on, “can-do” approach&lt;br&gt;• Strives in moving in a fast-paced environment, including handling multiple calls/demos per day with immediate follow-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Intermediate-level knowledge of Cloud platforms like Azure &amp;amp;amp; AWS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift Timing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The role requires working in the US time zone, with shift timings from 6:00 PM to 3:00 AM IST.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills And Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Experience with a SaaS company or demonstrable knowledge of SaaS practices&lt;br&gt;• Intermediate level of knowledge of cloud-native IaaS &amp;amp;amp; PaaS services.&lt;br&gt;• A high level of business acumen and experience working with various cross-&lt;br&gt;functional stakeholders to foster collaboration in solving business challenges&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Fundamental knowledge of the NIST Cybersecurity 2.0 framework&lt;br&gt;Basic knowledge of cybersecurity solutions in the areas of EDR, XDR, MDR, etc.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Professional Services Consultant has a responsibility to discover, design, consult, and implement Druva solutions for new and existing customers and provide best practices and guide the customer during the entire implementation cycle.&amp;nbsp; In addition, this would also include providing technical consultation on Druva’s Data Security Services and Disaster Recovery Services and conducting Cyber Simulations, Security assessments, assistance with Ransomware Recovery and Disaster Recovery Playbooks and Runbooks, configuration and integration of SIEM/SOAR tools, etc. As a member of the Professional Services team, this role will engage and drive customer success. Candidates for this pivotal position are highly dynamic and seasoned professionals with soft and technical skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Professional Services Consultant, you will interact with peers around the globe and be a mentor to your team. The ability to effectively scale your interactions from highly technical I.T. staff to key stakeholders at the Executive level is a must.&amp;nbsp; Flexibility in your current skill set and a demonstrable eagerness to learn new things are key criteria to any candidate for this position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work in a team of individual contributors who are empowered to make decisions and run their daily business tasks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discover, Design, Deploy, and Optimize Druva Solutions to meet customer requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end to end product deployments and configurations for all lines of business in Druva related to Enterprise Workloads, End User Protection, SaaS Applications and Ransomware and Disaster Recovery practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct Cyber Simulation exercises and Security assessments to test customer’s readiness to handle a cyber attack as well as identify gaps within existing security practices and provide recommendations to mitigate the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct Security Penetration testings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with Incident Response Plans, Recovery Playbooks and Cyber Recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with SIEM/SOAR integrations and configurations between the Customer and Druva’s environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Project Plans, and organize and manage all phases of a project to ensure successful implementation. This includes developing technical solutions and managing project plans, project schedules, success criteria, and milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult with customers and internal teams on best practices and meet expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate status to key stakeholders on project status to drive the outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timely responsiveness to customer satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage customer relationships and perform environmental health assessments of product adoption and data resiliency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams on customer requests and feature/product enhancements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in technical customer-facing roles with at least 2+ years as a Consultant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading and assisting the team and driving large customer implementation across all customers for Enterprise Workloads, End User protection, SaaS Applications, Ransomware Recovery, Disaster Recovery practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert level knowledge of Operating Systems including MS Windows, Linux and Mac.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with IDP, SSO Tools, SCCM/Casper/Jamf/intune Deployment tools, Virtual environments (VMWare, VMC, HyperV, AWS, Azure, Nutanix), Storage Technologies (SAN/NAS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Networking concepts (TCP/IP, DNS, Bandwidth Management, Firewalls), Cloud Technologies using AWS/Azure/M365/Google Workspace as well as Security Solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast Learner in a dynamic environment with changing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in conducting Cyber Simulation Exercises with multiple stakeholders&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in conducting Risk Assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in curating IR playbooks and runbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in handling a cyber recovery process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automation and scripting tools such as PowerShell, Python, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to API’s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Results-oriented with the ability to prioritize activities, plan and organize to meet commitments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent presentation, communication (verbal &amp;amp; written), and relationship-building skills, across all levels of management including negotiations and risk abatement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent consultative approach to customer engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SaaS demonstrating deep knowledge of SaaS practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a cross-functional team environment and collaborate with key partners to drive customer engagement and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of automation and scripting tools such as PowerShell, Python, etc would be an added advantage. .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of enterprise server backup technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working Knowledge and practical experience administrating Virtual Infrastructure.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backup &amp;amp; Restore of File, NAS, MSSQL,MYSQL, Oracle Servers, SAP HANA, AHV, VMware, EC2, Azure VM, VMC, Nutanix, EP, SFDC, M365, Gsuite etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working Knowledge of AWS services - mainly EC2, S3, RDS, IAM &amp;amp; VPC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience with conducting Cyber Simulation exercises to identify security vulnerabilities and provide recommendations to mitigate the gaps&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SIEM/SOAR tools and industry-wide ransomware recovery practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Blue team activities and its related tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of project management methodologies and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Storage protocols SAS, Fibre Channel, SCSI, iSCSI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of SaaS applications such as M365, Google Workspace, Salesforce etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Network Technologies and protocols – TCP/IP, VLAN, DNS, switches, firewalls, routers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of scripting languages such as PowerShell, Python etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISM or Security+ certified preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience Level:&lt;/strong&gt; 6–10 Years&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain:&lt;/strong&gt; Product Security / AppSec / DevSecOps / AI Security / AI-First SDLC&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Role Summary&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on &lt;strong&gt;Senior Staff Product Security Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join and lead initiatives across our product security landscape. In this role, you will redefine modern Product Security by architecting an AI-first SDLC seamlessly integrating traditional AppSec with advanced AI security practices, automating shift-left pipelines, conducting rigorous threat models for core services and complex AI architectures, and leveraging cutting-edge AI tools to accelerate vulnerability remediation. You will partner directly with engineering leadership, Information Security, GRC, BuildOps, and DevOps teams to secure our SaaS products and safely enable cutting-edge agentic features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Role &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-First SDLC &amp;amp; Shift-Left Automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect and embed AI-driven security controls (SAST, DAST, SCA, Container, Secrets Detection) directly into CI/CD build pipelines and developer workflows, establishing an intelligent, highly automated AI-first SDLC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational &amp;amp; Strategic AI Security:&lt;/strong&gt; Leverage AI tooling operationally (e.g., auto-triage, threat-model drafting, fix generation) while strategizing security controls for product-facing AI features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; Emerging Tech Threat Modeling:&lt;/strong&gt; Assess risks specific to Generative and Agentic AI architectures, including MCP integrations, autonomous agents, tool-calling interfaces, multi-agent communication, prompt injections, and memory/context poisoning (OWASP Top 10 for LLMs / Agentic Apps).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Guidance &amp;amp; Vulnerability Remediation:&lt;/strong&gt; Review code (Python, Go, Javascript, etc), triage findings, and partner with engineering to implement robust short and long-term security fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supply Chain &amp;amp; Software Integrity:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage third-party open-source risks, open-source dependency tracking, Software Bills of Materials (SBOMs), and secure MCP/agent server ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enablement &amp;amp; Champions Program:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct secure coding workshops, train developers on secure AI usage, and help grow an active Security Champions network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 6–10 years of product security engineering experience in a SaaS environment, with a proven track record of technical leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AppSec Fundamentals:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep expertise in OWASP Top 10, CWE 25, threat modeling, cryptography, container security, and secure SDLC frameworks (SAMM, Microsoft SDL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Security &amp;amp; AI-First SDLC Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong hands-on expertise with AI-first SDLC methodologies and reviewing AI security risks specifically around Agentic AI systems, MCP security (authorization, tool poisoning, confused deputy risks), and LLM security controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational AI Use-Cases:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience using AI tools to optimize security engineering workflows (e.g., automating root-cause analysis, threat modeling assistance, automated policy generation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming &amp;amp; Tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficient in code review and scripting with Python, Go, or Javascript (hands-on development experience is a major plus). Hands-on with tools like Burp Suite, Snyk, OWASP ZAP, and CI/CD security scanners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree in CS/IT or equivalent. Relevant certifications (OSCP, OSWE, CSSLP, GIAC) or active community contributions (OWASP, BSides, NullCon, Black Hat, etc) are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;About Druva:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won&#39;t just join a company at Druva; you&#39;ll help shape the future of data security at the moment it matters most. We are building a modern standard with our cloud-native solutions, designed to simplify the toughest challenges in cyber resilience for our customers. As the pioneer and market leader in fully managed SaaS data protection, we help organizations secure and recover their data from ransomware, cyberattacks, and operational disruptions without the complexity, cost, or risk of legacy infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our momentum is backed by the market: Druva was named a &lt;strong&gt;Leader in the 2026 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™ for Backup and Data Protection Platforms&lt;/strong&gt;, a &lt;strong&gt;Leader in the IDC MarketScape for Cyber-Recovery&lt;/strong&gt;, and a &lt;strong&gt;Leader &amp;amp; Outperformer in the GigaOm Cloud Data Protection Radar&lt;/strong&gt;. Even better, customers validate that leadership every day through standout Net Promoter Scores (NPS) and Gartner Peer Insights ratings. Today, the platform protects over &lt;strong&gt;450PB of customer data across 26 global regions&lt;/strong&gt; and runs more than &lt;strong&gt;7 billion backups a year&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://druva.com/&quot; data-external-url=&quot;https://druva.com&quot; data-requires-redirect=&quot;true&quot;&gt;druva.com&lt;/a&gt; and follow us on LinkedIn, X, and Facebook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;team-mission-druva-product-platform&quot;&gt;Team &amp;amp; Mission: Druva Product Platform&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Druva Product Platform&lt;/strong&gt; team builds the shared core SaaS foundation that every Druva product line runs on. We build and operate the multi-tenant control plane, distributed APIs, tenant lifecycle and provisioning pipelines, Identity &amp;amp; Access Management (IAM/RBAC), distributed job orchestration, usage metering, and platform observability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When a new workload or product capability ships at Druva, it ships on top of what this team owns. That makes the work high-leverage and high-blast-radius: our services are multi-tenant, globally distributed, always-on, and measured against strict availability and latency objectives at a scale of thousands of enterprise customers and billions of operations per year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;role-overview&quot;&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer (Development)&lt;/strong&gt; on the Druva Product Platform team, you will be a core backend engineer responsible for designing, developing, scaling, and operating critical multi-tenant microservices and APIs. You will own complex technical deliverables end-to-end—from architectural documents and high-performance Go/Python implementations to automated CI/CD deployments and production telemetry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on individual contributor role for an engineer who thrives on distributed systems challenges, concurrency, high data throughput, and building foundational platform services that empower other engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;key-skills&quot;&gt;Key Skills:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5–8+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of hands-on experience in software product development, building high-scale distributed systems and SaaS backends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;Go (Golang)&lt;/strong&gt; and/or &lt;strong&gt;Python&lt;/strong&gt;, with deep understanding of concurrency (goroutines/async I/O), memory management, and data structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience in designing, building, and maintaining &lt;strong&gt;microservices and REST/gRPC APIs&lt;/strong&gt; in high-throughput multi-tenant environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience with &lt;strong&gt;AWS Cloud services&lt;/strong&gt; (such as EKS, EC2, S3, DynamoDB, RDS, SQS, SNS, Lambda) and containerization (&lt;strong&gt;Docker, Kubernetes&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong database expertise across relational engines (PostgreSQL/MySQL) and distributed NoSQL databases (DynamoDB, Redis, Elasticsearch).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with event-driven architectures and message streaming systems (Apache Kafka, AWS SQS/EventBridge).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of services in production: telemetry/instrumentation (Prometheus, OpenTelemetry, Datadog), SLI/SLO monitoring, on-call support, and root cause analysis (RCA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid commitment to lean engineering practices: automated unit/integration testing, CI/CD pipelines, and rigorous peer code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;desirable-skills&quot;&gt;Desirable Skills:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building multi-tenant platform primitives: tenant isolation, rate limiting/token buckets, quota management, and schema migrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain expertise in data protection, backup/recovery, storage systems, virtualization, or cyber resilience (RPO/RTO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of enterprise authentication and authorization standards (OAuth 2.0, SAML, OIDC, RBAC/ABAC, mTLS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to AI/LLM integration patterns (vector search, prompt engineering pipelines, LLM agent integration).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-growth, fast-paced SaaS product environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;role-and-responsibilities&quot;&gt;Role and Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, implement, and maintain high-performance, resilient microservices in Go/Python that serve as the backbone for Druva&#39;s SaaS platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design clean, backward-compatible, secure RESTful and gRPC APIs consumed by internal product engineering teams and enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author clear technical design documents evaluating architectural trade-offs across latency, consistency, scalability, and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize database queries, caching strategies, and data models across PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, and Redis for sub-millisecond responsiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive production operational excellence: set up granular telemetry (metrics, traces, logs), define SLOs, and participate in on-call incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct blameless root cause analyses (RCAs) for production issues and ship permanent software mitigations to eliminate recurring failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Managers, Architects, and Quality Engineers to break down business requirements into deliverable engineering milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion code quality and engineering best practices: perform in-depth code reviews and maintain high automated test coverage (&amp;gt;85%).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and coach junior engineers, fostering technical excellence, design rigor, and continuous learning across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;qualification&quot;&gt;Qualification:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.Tech / B.E / M.E / M.Tech in Computer Science, Information Technology, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

